{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update16.json\",\"summary\":\"Corrected the completion comparison's admission and requested a successor execution, while recording the first extended run honestly. Receipt e5527cca0ee64fd681d3ec1371f9cca6 (successor experiment 6ba3fb0618b64be7aa792b0f450b9cbf-experiment) had its re-queue comparison hold but its completion comparison come back unknown because the admission event described instance (0,0) while the reply observation describes the re-proposed instance (0,1) - a harness observation-construction defect, not target behaviour; the successor now admits on the re-proposed instance's decided state. The account records the measured chain from that run's event stream (the re-queued proposal creating instance (0,1), that instance reaching COMMITTED, the package's own execution entry point returning true with a 17-byte reply, and the decoded reply carrying command id 77 with ok 1) and flags that the measured completion claim currently rests on the parsed events rather than on a declared comparison outcome. The reply-side gap is answered as resolved: the replaced instance itself produces no reply because handleCommit cleared the owner's proposals while the execution-time reply condition requires them, whereas the re-proposed instance serves the completion. The re-propose behavior now cites both receipts' indices, and its narrow cases (non-NONE replacement, failed owner, batching, harness-invoked entry point) stay in the counterevidence and limits.\"}"}}
